BT /F1 10.0 Tf 50.0 790.0 Td (Question: A simply supported beam carries a 10 kN point load at midspan over a 6 m span. Find) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.0 Tf 50.0 776.0 Td (each support reaction.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.0 Tf 50.0 762.0 Td (1. Draw the free-body diagram with vertical reactions RA and RB.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.0 Tf 50.0 748.0 Td (2. Use vertical equilibrium: RA + RB - 10 = 0 kN.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.0 Tf 50.0 734.0 Td (3. Take moments about A: RB\(6\) - 10\(3\) = 0, so RB = 5 kN; then RA = 5 kN.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.0 Tf 50.0 720.0 Td (Answer: Each support reaction is 5 kN upward.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.0 Tf 50.0 706.0 Td (Check: The reactions sum to 10 kN and their moments balance about either support.) Tj ET
